{title: Out of the Depths}
{subtitle: Psalm 130}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Out of the depths I cry to you, O Lord
Lord, hear my voice
Let your ears be attentive
To my cry for mercy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My [Bb]soul waits for the [Cm]Lord
More [Bb]than watchmen for the morn[Cm]ing
More [Bb]than watchmen for the morn[Cm]ing [Bb][Cm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If you, Lord, kept a record of sins
Lord, who could stand
But with you there is forgiveness
And in your word I hold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My soul [Bb]waits for the [Cm]Lord
More than [Bb]watchmen for the morn[Cm]ing
More than [Bb]watchmen for the morn[Cm]ing
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
With the Lord there is steadfast love
{end_of_verse}
